  "instructions": [
    "Heat the niter kibbeh in a large saucepan over medium heat.",
    "Add the onion and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened and caramelized, about 20 minutes.",
    "Add the garlic, ginger, red pepper flakes, cumin, coriander, turmeric, paprika, salt, and black pepper to the saucepan and cook, stirring constantly, for 1 minute.",
    "Add the baby plum tomatoes to the saucepan and cook, stirring occasionally, until they start to break down and release their juices, about 10 minutes.",
    "Use an immersion blender to puree the mixture to your desired consistency.",
    "Serve the Misir Wot over bread or injera."
  ],
